  "visualBrief": "Individual palace quadrangle with native courtyard voids, pale Portland-stone three-pediment east facade in 3:7:3:7:3 bay rhythm, rusticated low storey/mezzanines, real arched carriage passages, divided sash glazing and giant Corinthian orders. Continuous first-floor balustrade and ceremonial balcony, pierced rooftop balustrade, original simplified pediment relief and bare flagstaff. Distinct warm Bath-stone garden front with engaged-column five-window bow, shallow green copper half dome, tall attic, giant-column pavilions, raised terrace/balustrades and conservatory. Attached palace wings/ballroom, courtyard porticoes and Ambassadors’ Court temple porch. Separate Royal Mews, memorial, gates, neighbors, people, interiors and photo textures excluded.",
